WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:00.983
- What's up guys?

00:00:00.983 --> 00:00:02.800
Today I have an amazing video for you

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:03.949
where we're going to be talking about

00:00:03.949 --> 00:00:05.859
all of your most
frequently asked questions

00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:08.283
on the COVID-19 vaccination.

00:00:08.283 --> 00:00:11.560
I brought an amazing
guest, Dr. Seema Yasmin.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:12.840
Who's not only a doctor,

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.904
she's an epidemiologist, a journalist.

00:00:14.904 --> 00:00:16.723
She's the director of
research and education

00:00:16.723 --> 00:00:19.980
at the Stanford Health
Communication Initiative.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.300
Dr. Yasmin, thank you
so much for being here.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.570
We're really excited to have you.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:24.570
- I'm really excited.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:26.860
Thanks so much Dr. Mike
for having me on today.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.499
- Everyone is hearing about the vaccine.

00:00:28.499 --> 00:00:30.270
When do you think

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:32.039
that we can actually
start giving this vaccine

00:00:32.039 --> 00:00:35.258
to everybody outside of
frontline healthcare workers

00:00:35.258 --> 00:00:39.290
and those who are over the
age specified by the CDC?

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.248
- As of mid to late December

00:00:41.248 --> 00:00:43.571
we got two different COVID-19 vaccines

00:00:43.571 --> 00:00:46.174
with an emergency use
authorization in the U.S.

00:00:46.174 --> 00:00:49.660
But more coming I think
in the next few weeks.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.099
The point at which you can
start to extend vaccination

00:00:52.099 --> 00:00:53.377
to many more people,

00:00:53.377 --> 00:00:55.677
the tens of millions
that we need vaccinated,

00:00:55.677 --> 00:00:57.730
could be a few months away.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:58.794
There are strong projections

00:00:58.794 --> 00:01:00.340
that it could be around April time.

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:03.725
I think saying spring to summer
is fair because bear in mind

00:01:03.725 --> 00:01:05.599
that at least for the two vaccines

00:01:05.599 --> 00:01:07.520
we have currently available,

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.740
it's not just a one and done shot.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.044
You're having to go back
three or four weeks later

00:01:12.044 --> 00:01:13.760
depending on which one you got.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:15.311
And even then it's only one to two weeks

00:01:15.311 --> 00:01:17.078
after your second shot

00:01:17.078 --> 00:01:20.055
that your body's actually
develop that kind of immunity,

00:01:20.055 --> 00:01:22.026
that's going to protect
you from getting sick.

00:01:22.026 --> 00:01:23.402
- Should there be a preference

00:01:23.402 --> 00:01:26.210
to which ones our
countries should be buying?

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:28.430
Are you allowed to mix the vaccines?

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:29.667
- Some people may get a choice

00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:32.360
like, "Hey we have this
a buffet of vaccine."

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:35.550
I think for some realistically
that won't be so much choice.

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:37.750
But now I think when you are told

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:39.920
you are eligible for a particular vaccine,

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.600
I would roll up your sleeve
and go for what's available.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:45.160
We don't have any data
on mixing and matching.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:46.256
So that means if your first shot

00:01:46.256 --> 00:01:48.250
is the Pfizer BioNTech shot,

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:51.420
you should get that as your
second shot three weeks later.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:52.992
If your first shot was the Moderna one,

00:01:52.992 --> 00:01:55.900
that should be your second
shot four weeks later.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:57.060
- We're still humans.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.040
Errors are going to be made.

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:01.745
I just read a press article
of a pharmacist I believe

00:02:01.745 --> 00:02:04.931
that was given multiple doses
of the vaccine accidentally

00:02:04.931 --> 00:02:08.250
because they didn't know it
came in a multi-dose vial.

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.796
And things like that are part
of real-world applications.

00:02:10.796 --> 00:02:12.360
These things are gonna happen.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.760
Yeah, we shouldn't be set
back by one piece of bad news.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:17.603
And I know the press a
lot of times will do that

00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:19.830
and make it seem like
something is horrible.

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:20.663
- I want people to know

00:02:20.663 --> 00:02:21.820
that some people don't feel very well.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:23.484
Some have to take a day
off work the next day.

00:02:23.484 --> 00:02:24.381
If you know that,

00:02:24.381 --> 00:02:27.777
it's less scary going in
should it happen to you.

00:02:27.777 --> 00:02:29.678
However, the flip side of that

00:02:29.678 --> 00:02:31.948
is that every single time

00:02:31.948 --> 00:02:35.024
someone on the planet has
had an allergic reaction

00:02:35.024 --> 00:02:37.240
to one of these COVID-19 vaccines,

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:40.560
it's become a big headline.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.443
And I know people that are like,

00:02:41.443 --> 00:02:42.622
"Oh, I'm just really scared."

00:02:42.622 --> 00:02:44.390
And I'm like, "Hold on."

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:46.543
A few million people

00:02:46.543 --> 00:02:49.153
at this point have received these vaccines

00:02:49.153 --> 00:02:51.587
and about eight I think at my last count,

00:02:51.587 --> 00:02:53.044
you know, less than a dozen

00:02:53.044 --> 00:02:55.500
have developed an allergic reaction.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.181
You are totally allowed
to be scared of that.

00:02:57.181 --> 00:03:00.520
Allergic reactions are scary,
but all of them were fine.

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:01.833
They got treated.

00:03:01.833 --> 00:03:03.238
And this is the very reason that,

00:03:03.238 --> 00:03:05.991
after you get any
vaccine for the most part

00:03:05.991 --> 00:03:07.285
you're not allowed to
go home straight away

00:03:07.285 --> 00:03:09.201
even though you want to get
back to work or whatever.

00:03:09.201 --> 00:03:10.425
You're told, "No.

00:03:10.425 --> 00:03:12.837
Please sit in the waiting room
for the next 15, 30 minutes

00:03:12.837 --> 00:03:14.690
in case you have a reaction."

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:16.987
Because this vaccine was
produced rather quickly,

00:03:16.987 --> 00:03:20.258
we haven't had the longterm
side effect research available

00:03:20.258 --> 00:03:22.800
on it, simply because the
time hasn't been there.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:25.167
Is there anything in your
mind that would suggest

00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:27.860
that there are serious
long-term side effects?

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:29.759
- If you look at the history of vaccines

00:03:29.759 --> 00:03:31.511
and reactions to vaccines,

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:35.170
the vast majority if
not nearly all of them

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:38.680
occur within the days
after you get vaccinated

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:42.780
or at most about four to
five weeks after vaccination.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:45.513
So we put safety data beyond
that amount of time, right?

00:03:45.513 --> 00:03:48.480
We've got at least eight
weeks of safety data,

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:50.155
but the other thing to bear in mind

00:03:50.155 --> 00:03:52.173
is that we haven't just dropped the ball

00:03:52.173 --> 00:03:55.180
now that we have emergency
use authorization

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:56.330
of these vaccines.

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:59.500
We are continuing to monitor
people for years out.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:01.864
And also another thing is,
remember, we're prioritizing

00:04:01.864 --> 00:04:05.960
especially in the UK older
people to get vaccinated.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:07.027
And so we're going to be hearing stories

00:04:07.027 --> 00:04:09.200
and I want to give everyone
a heads up of this,

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.762
of folks saying, "Well,
my granddad was 85.

00:04:11.762 --> 00:04:14.120
He got the COVID 19 vaccine

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.980
and then he died the next month."

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:18.283
The thing is, if you are in your eighties,

00:04:18.283 --> 00:04:22.010
you have a 1 in 10, 1 in 12 roughly chance

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:24.090
of dying in the next year.

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:26.371
And so just because you're
in that high priority group

00:04:26.371 --> 00:04:27.930
to get the vaccine,

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:30.330
it might look like
increased deaths occurring

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:31.460
in that population.

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:33.420
- How does this vaccine work

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:36.244
and why is it different
than the flu vaccine

00:04:36.244 --> 00:04:39.140
or other vaccinations that
we've heard so much about?

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:41.234
- So all vaccines are
trying to do the same thing.

00:04:41.234 --> 00:04:44.048
They're trying to give your
immune system a heads up

00:04:44.048 --> 00:04:46.539
to be prepared should you ever be exposed

00:04:46.539 --> 00:04:48.750
to the actual virus.

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:50.238
With these two mRNA vaccine,

00:04:50.238 --> 00:04:54.350
so there's one made by Pfizer
BioNTech one made by Moderna,

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:55.183
they are new technology.

00:04:55.183 --> 00:04:57.216
They're doing something really amazing

00:04:57.216 --> 00:05:00.243
where they're giving your
body a little piece of RNA

00:05:00.243 --> 00:05:03.970
which is the genetic
code that your body needs

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:07.768
for your own cells to start
making little tiny fragments

00:05:07.768 --> 00:05:09.910
of this new Coronavirus.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:11.662
So your body's not making the whole virus.

00:05:11.662 --> 00:05:14.285
You can't get any
infections from the vaccine,

00:05:14.285 --> 00:05:18.078
but your body gets the code to
make just the spike protein.

00:05:18.078 --> 00:05:19.756
And then by making that protein,

00:05:19.756 --> 00:05:22.194
your immune system sees it, takes note.

00:05:22.194 --> 00:05:23.732
It's like, "Okay going to get ready

00:05:23.732 --> 00:05:26.300
should we ever get exposed to this."

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:27.133
In the meantime,

00:05:27.133 --> 00:05:30.190
that RNA that got injected
into you from the vaccine,

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:31.163
it disappears quite quickly.

00:05:31.163 --> 00:05:32.660
It's very fragile.

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:34.411
- Re-iterating what you said
'cause it's so important.

00:05:34.411 --> 00:05:36.742
You're not making the full virus.

00:05:36.742 --> 00:05:40.863
So you cannot get COVID-19
by getting the vaccine.

00:05:40.863 --> 00:05:43.501
- The incredible thing
about these newer vaccines,

00:05:43.501 --> 00:05:47.165
is that they don't contain
any portion of live,

00:05:47.165 --> 00:05:49.840
weakened or dead virus,

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.120
which is how some other vaccines work.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.695
- What are the ingredients of the vaccine?

00:05:53.695 --> 00:05:55.260
And are they trustworthy?

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:56.937
- Some of the questions
I get asked the most are,

00:05:56.937 --> 00:05:58.932
is there anything toxic in there?

00:05:58.932 --> 00:06:00.243
And is there aluminium

00:06:00.243 --> 00:06:02.372
or aluminum as you would say in the U.S.

00:06:02.372 --> 00:06:04.654
The list actually of
ingredients in these vaccines

00:06:04.654 --> 00:06:05.616
it's publicly available.

00:06:05.616 --> 00:06:07.420
You can go online and see it.

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:08.253
It's quite a short list

00:06:08.253 --> 00:06:10.633
and there is no mercury
and no aluminum in them.

00:06:10.633 --> 00:06:12.231
- And the important part is,

00:06:12.231 --> 00:06:15.650
just because there's a
chemical name to a substance,

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:18.904
it doesn't make it
automatically bad or dangerous.

00:06:18.904 --> 00:06:20.760
And on the flip side,

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:22.732
if something has claimed to be all natural

00:06:22.732 --> 00:06:24.780
doesn't mean that it's all safe.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:27.720
How effective do we think
this vaccine is going to be?

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:28.561
Let's not talk real-world,

00:06:28.561 --> 00:06:31.300
let's talk based on the
evidence we have thus far.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:32.412
- In the clinical trials,

00:06:32.412 --> 00:06:34.083
in those phase three clinical trials

00:06:34.083 --> 00:06:38.620
which was 44,000 people for
the Pfizer BioNTech trial

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:42.350
and about 30,400 for the Moderna trial,

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:44.733
these vaccines were found
to be very efficacious.

00:06:44.733 --> 00:06:46.990
And I'll say efficacious, not effective

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:49.640
'cause they're talking
about in a clinical trial.

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:53.570
But around 94 to 95% efficacious,

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:56.650
that was way more than we expected.

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:57.500
And specifically

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:59.750
when we're talking about
those numbers of efficacy,

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:03.340
we're talking about the
reduced likelihood of a person

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:05.830
becoming sick with COVID-19.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:09.160
Were not talking about a reduced chance

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:11.921
of getting the infection and
therefore a reduced chance

00:07:11.921 --> 00:07:14.870
of spreading it to other people.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:17.870
That transmissibility
part that question about

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:20.132
if I get this vaccine,
am I less contagious?

00:07:20.132 --> 00:07:22.763
Unfortunately, the clinical
trials we have so far

00:07:22.763 --> 00:07:25.728
did not seek to answer that question.

00:07:25.728 --> 00:07:29.220
That's something we're going
to learn from the real world.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:32.093
- How soon after we're
vaccinated, both doses

00:07:32.093 --> 00:07:36.020
are we considered
protected to this 90, 95%.

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:37.242
- It takes one to two weeks

00:07:37.242 --> 00:07:40.404
for your body to build up that
immunity against the virus.

00:07:40.404 --> 00:07:41.994
- How many people need to get this vaccine

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:44.850
in order for it to be
considered like eradicated?

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:48.890
- We think about 70, maybe 75% or so

00:07:48.890 --> 00:07:51.950
of Americans would need to be vaccinated

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:53.333
in order for us to achieve

00:07:53.333 --> 00:07:54.930
that herd immunity that we talk about.

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:56.304
But it's still a big chunk.

00:07:56.304 --> 00:07:58.101
We are talking about
three out of four people.

00:07:58.101 --> 00:07:59.493
- How much will it cost?

00:07:59.493 --> 00:08:02.410
Do I need health insurance
in order to be vaccinated?

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:04.060
- No cost to individuals

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:06.848
whether you are insured
or you are not insured.

00:08:06.848 --> 00:08:09.518
The vaccines themselves
can be quite expensive,

00:08:09.518 --> 00:08:12.810
but remember the billions
it's cost to get us here,

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:14.914
that's largely taxpayer money.

00:08:14.914 --> 00:08:17.120
So we paid for these.

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:19.886
Now it's the government's
job to distribute them fairly

00:08:19.886 --> 00:08:22.910
and to make sure everyone who
needs a vaccine can get one.

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:25.170
- What's the official recommendations

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:26.780
for who should get this vaccine?

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:29.600
Are there groups that we
recommend shouldn't take it?

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:31.839
- So right now I'm not seeing
too many recommendations

00:08:31.839 --> 00:08:34.826
about who should be
excluded from vaccination.

00:08:34.826 --> 00:08:36.690
There's some kind of gray areas,

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:39.020
for example around pregnant women,

00:08:39.020 --> 00:08:40.837
because unfortunately and
I think this is not great

00:08:40.837 --> 00:08:44.350
but they weren't included
in the clinical trials.

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:46.482
And so it means pregnant
women are kind of told

00:08:46.482 --> 00:08:49.320
you can if you want,
to talk to your doctor,

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:50.337
weigh the risk of infection

00:08:50.337 --> 00:08:53.300
versus potential risk of vaccination

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:54.266
and then make up your mind.

00:08:54.266 --> 00:08:56.320
That's not clear cut guidance.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:58.460
The other question that
comes up is should groups

00:08:58.460 --> 00:09:01.099
who are immunocompromised
not receive these vaccines?

00:09:01.099 --> 00:09:03.457
And actually we're saying you
can receive these vaccines

00:09:03.457 --> 00:09:04.950
because they don't contain the virus

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:08.240
like from other different
kinds of vaccines do.

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:10.520
- And then what about children?

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:13.810
You know, generally they have
fared better with this virus.

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:15.078
They are still vectors for it,

00:09:15.078 --> 00:09:16.850
and potentially can be spreading.

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:18.690
- When you don't have
that clinical trial data

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:21.373
from children it makes
it really hard to say

00:09:21.373 --> 00:09:23.764
what you should do for children at large.

00:09:23.764 --> 00:09:26.132
The good news is Moderna is now recruiting

00:09:26.132 --> 00:09:28.830
for a clinical trial for its vaccine

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:30.567
among 12 to 17 year olds.

00:09:30.567 --> 00:09:33.058
So I hope in the next few
months, that gives us that data

00:09:33.058 --> 00:09:35.264
about how should children be involved.

00:09:35.264 --> 00:09:37.492
- This is so important to state here,

00:09:37.492 --> 00:09:41.430
that the reason this
vaccine is being recommended

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:43.193
for groups 16 and older, is
not because we have evidence

00:09:43.193 --> 00:09:46.241
that it's harmful for
those who are under 16,

00:09:46.241 --> 00:09:50.540
it's because simply we
do not have full efficacy

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:54.067
and we haven't tested it in
groups under the age of 16.

00:09:54.067 --> 00:09:57.400
And I think now is a really
good time to talk about

00:09:57.400 --> 00:09:58.465
the difference between

00:09:58.465 --> 00:10:02.340
those who are truly anti-vax activists

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:04.060
or anti-vaccine activists

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:06.662
and those who are vaccine hesitant,

00:10:06.662 --> 00:10:09.541
because they've heard something,
they've read something

00:10:09.541 --> 00:10:13.180
that's potentially
misinformation or disinformation.

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:15.067
- I'm so glad you worded
it that way as well Mike

00:10:15.067 --> 00:10:17.206
because I think I try actually not to use

00:10:17.206 --> 00:10:19.710
the term anti-vaccine very much.

00:10:19.710 --> 00:10:22.481
The vast majority of
people who are kind of

00:10:22.481 --> 00:10:24.141
a bit worried about these vaccines,

00:10:24.141 --> 00:10:26.453
they're not what you people
might call anti-vaxers

00:10:26.453 --> 00:10:28.460
they're vaccine hesitant.

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:29.627
They're the kinds of folks who are like,

00:10:29.627 --> 00:10:31.616
"Yeah my kids got all
their childhood vaccines.

00:10:31.616 --> 00:10:33.069
Normally get my flu shot.

00:10:33.069 --> 00:10:35.559
I'm just not too sure
about these new ones.

00:10:35.559 --> 00:10:38.220
They seem to have been
developed a bit quickly."

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:40.970
Those are the people we really
need to be reaching out to.

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:43.367
And actually specifically
that question about,

00:10:43.367 --> 00:10:44.200
"Wait, you told me,

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:47.341
normally it takes about
10 years on average

00:10:47.341 --> 00:10:48.970
to develop a vaccine,

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:50.182
then how could it happen in 10 months?"

00:10:50.182 --> 00:10:51.270
The question should be

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:54.972
why does it normally take us
10 years to develop a vaccine?

00:10:54.972 --> 00:10:56.920
That's way too long.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:59.260
What's happened in the last 10 months

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:01.580
is proof of what can get done,

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:03.882
how amazing science can be done

00:11:03.882 --> 00:11:05.228
and what achievements you get

00:11:05.228 --> 00:11:07.509
when you have international collaboration

00:11:07.509 --> 00:11:10.226
and literally tens of billions of dollars

00:11:10.226 --> 00:11:11.577
thrown at the problem.

00:11:11.577 --> 00:11:13.450
But the other piece of context is,

00:11:13.450 --> 00:11:15.485
I know this virus is brand new,

00:11:15.485 --> 00:11:18.536
but the researchers who
brought us these vaccines

00:11:18.536 --> 00:11:22.573
have been working on this
kind of scenario for years.

00:11:22.573 --> 00:11:25.320
So that university of
Oxford group for example,

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:28.260
have been working on a
vaccine for pandemic X,

00:11:28.260 --> 00:11:30.290
a virus potentially that comes along.

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:31.567
That is brand new.

00:11:31.567 --> 00:11:33.860
What they've been working
on for a few years,

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:35.885
is how do we get 10 steps ahead of that?

00:11:35.885 --> 00:11:39.229
So that when this nali infection arises,

00:11:39.229 --> 00:11:42.160
we have to do very little
work to make a vaccine.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:43.882
- This is an international effort

00:11:43.882 --> 00:11:46.103
where everyone is on the same page.

00:11:46.103 --> 00:11:48.815
We're cutting out a lot
of bureaucratic red tape

00:11:48.815 --> 00:11:50.630
to put it simply, right.

00:11:50.630 --> 00:11:51.940
Like in getting the funding.

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:52.773
Why?

00:11:52.773 --> 00:11:54.340
Because our economy was threatened.

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:56.167
Anytime you threatened
the economy or money,

00:11:56.167 --> 00:11:59.070
the problem usually gets
solved a lot quicker

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:00.538
in a more efficacious way.

00:12:00.538 --> 00:12:02.244
I think this antibody conversation

00:12:02.244 --> 00:12:04.845
has been really confusing
to the general public.

00:12:04.845 --> 00:12:07.737
Because A, we can test for the antibodies.

00:12:07.737 --> 00:12:10.760
We don't know what the cutoff
is to know that you're immune.

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:11.723
We don't know how long it lasts.

00:12:11.723 --> 00:12:14.330
We kind of have this
arbitrary three month cutoff.

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:16.166
- The kind of immunity that you get

00:12:16.166 --> 00:12:18.790
from some vaccines can be stronger

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:22.890
and longer lasting than what
you get from natural infection.

00:12:22.890 --> 00:12:24.614
We also don't have amazing antibody test.

00:12:24.614 --> 00:12:27.050
Some of them and not the most specific

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:28.438
and the most sensitive.

00:12:28.438 --> 00:12:30.807
So there's been a lot of confusion around,

00:12:30.807 --> 00:12:32.190
who's been exposed?

00:12:32.190 --> 00:12:33.201
- I've actually had some debates

00:12:33.201 --> 00:12:35.310
with fellow physician friends of mine

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:38.234
who I've basically taken
a firmer stance in saying

00:12:38.234 --> 00:12:41.090
that I don't see a value for an individual

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:43.430
to go get tested for antibodies.

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:44.550
Do you agree with that?
- I agree.

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:45.650
Whenever you order a test,

00:12:45.650 --> 00:12:48.088
it's your responsibility to
follow up on their result,

00:12:48.088 --> 00:12:49.790
med school 101,

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:52.300
and also think about what's actionable.

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:53.890
We don't have a full understanding yet

00:12:53.890 --> 00:12:58.470
of what level of antibodies
truly confer resistance,

00:12:58.470 --> 00:13:01.468
truly confer protection
against this virus.

00:13:01.468 --> 00:13:03.985
So to me, there are still many unknowns.

00:13:03.985 --> 00:13:05.677
It's interesting from like a

00:13:05.677 --> 00:13:09.087
theoretical research perspective
to gather that data now,

00:13:09.087 --> 00:13:11.795
but in terms of telling a
patient what to do or not to do,

00:13:11.795 --> 00:13:13.946
I don't think antibodies
change that conversation.

00:13:13.946 --> 00:13:16.490
- If you questions about the vaccine,

00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:17.463
drop your questions down below.

00:13:17.463 --> 00:13:19.852
If you have any hesitations
drop them down below.

00:13:19.852 --> 00:13:21.368
I'm going to be trying to be more active

00:13:21.368 --> 00:13:23.620
in this common section versus others,

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:25.790
'cause I know a lot of
folks do have questions.

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:27.830
Dr. Yasmin, thank you
so much for being here

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:28.904
for all the work that you've done.

00:13:28.904 --> 00:13:30.169
Not only with COVID-19,

00:13:30.169 --> 00:13:32.680
but all the diseases you've investigated.

00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:34.150
Where can people follow you?

00:13:34.150 --> 00:13:35.268
Where can they stay up to date?

00:13:35.268 --> 00:13:36.892
- Well, thank you so much
for having me on today.

00:13:36.892 --> 00:13:39.283
Folks can follow me on
Twitter @DoctorYasmin

00:13:39.283 --> 00:13:42.080
and on Instagram at @DrSeemaYasmin.

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:42.913
- Thank you for being here

00:13:42.913 --> 00:13:44.718
and as always stay happy and healthy.

00:13:44.718 --> 00:13:47.385
